  },
  "notes": [
    "Hole geometry is the defining dimension of a plate, so it is recorded wherever it is published: mounting_hole_spacing_mm holds exact [W, D] pairs, mounting_hole_spacing_note holds the ranged or asymmetric values.",
    "B1, K and L each publish two Schematic Drawing sheets; alternate_drawing is the second one, kept as a -alt file in ref/quickmounts.",
    "dimensions_w_x_h_mm with geometry_source \"product-spec\" comes from the product page; \"drawing\" is read off the outline in the OEM drawing and carries no tolerance.",
    "No plate may be cut, sawn, or permanently modified during measurement; the on-hand plates stay usable."
  ]
}
